{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "chain-nonhaptog-runspec",
    "description": "PLAN.md §7.5 step 7d: the `chain-nonhaptog` RunSpec. Its 540 rows are IDENTICAL to `chain-tog-speciation`'s to the last digit -- the two snapshots agree at a relative 0.0 over all 540 cells -- so it cost no model change, exactly as `process-brakewear` cost none against `process-tirewear`. It is kept for the one thing it does discriminate.\n\nWHAT IT DISCRIMINATES (§23). IT SELECTS A SIXTH POLLUTANT-PROCESS AND EMITS FIVE BLOCKS. `runspecpollutantprocess` carries 8801 -- non-HAP TOG -- and the run emits nothing for it: it has no rate table row, no chain edge in `runspecchainedto`, and therefore no way to be computed. §69's rule is that such a pollutant-process is not emitted, and this is the run that says the rule survives a chain three rungs deep: the same document that must NOT drop TOG for want of a rate must drop non-HAP TOG for want of one.\n\n540 rows, worst cell 8.135e-06.",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"
    ],
    "tags": [
      "runspec",
      "onroad",
      "default-database",
      "chain-nonhaptog",
      "hc-speciation",
      "chained",
      "ragged"
    ]
  },
  "data_sources": {
    "db_runspecyear": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "../../moves.rs/characterization/snapshots/chain-nonhaptog/tables/db__movesexecution1ccc0232_campuscluster_illinois_edu__runspecyear.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_runspecyear"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "scope"
        ],
        "note": "1 row, yearID 2020. The scope comes from these tables and never from the RunSpec XML, whose @key attributes are 0-based indices into sorted ID lists (docs/mixed-onroad.md §0.1).",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
